Let $(X,\Mf,\mu)$ be a measure space. We say that this space is \it{separable}
if there exists a \it{countable} collection of sets $\{E_n\}_{n=1}^oo\subset\Mf$
such that for every $A\in\Fc$ and any $\epsilon>0$ there exists $n$ such that
$$
    ||\I_A - \I_{E_n}||_1 = \int_X |\I_A - \I_{E_n}|d\mu < \epsilon.
$$

